	<section_number>46.2-807</section_number>
	<catch_line>Path of travel at circular intersections</catch_line>
	<text>
		A vehicle passing through a circular intersection shall be driven only to the right of the central island, unless otherwise directed by traffic control devices.
	</text>
	<history>Code 1950, § 46-220.1; 1952, c. 671; 1958, c. 541, § 46.1-204; 1989, c. 727; 2013, cc. 128, 400.</history>
